perts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-f102687cd1ea46f5"], "revision": 7, "summary": "WAKE✳︎ ensures accountability by strictly coupling future research paths to the durable record of past consequences, treating governance as the immutable mechanism of continuity.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "d02b329e712b7369176e3106adeb01290f4b5e7d9ddd089e644e5a3461e59385", "hash": "14ee35c533f908dcf849c885cf11d1f7e9218403f4f5ef36b72ba461d3205ef7"}, {"seq": 5673, "time": "2026-10-31T11:59:57.135997+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 32831, "provider_input_hash": "fb99bdbd1349450c65f811e6b6632af7b801e7738fafd9e2f7b6e81d7690d1ad", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-64d5c82234434eb7"}, "prev_hash": "14ee35c533f908dcf849c885cf11d1f7e9218403f4f5ef36b72ba461d3205ef7", "hash": "74974507e615c695504ece1c8f6caafb1cefe571d1eff1974e0249cb72b72017"}, {"seq": 5674, "time": "2026-10-31T12:00:34.443296+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 32831, "provider_input_hash": "fb99bdbd1349450c65f811e6b6632af7b801e7738fafd9e2f7b6e81d7690d1ad", "result": "rate_limited", "retry_after_seconds": 40.75971579551697}, "effect_accounting": 1, "id": "w-64d5c82234434eb7"}, "prev_hash": "74974507e615c695504ece1c8f6caafb1cefe571d1eff1974e0249cb72b72017", "hash": "b1a781eb6eba32ada535fee66ddd098d454c74